    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-87529",
      "sequence_position": 4,
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14215685/assets/98ae486b18ff78601faf8a99f5310df982a73f0403ecf43186eef947b847bed4.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the function $y=f(x).$ Which of the following gives the graph of $y=\\frac{1}{2}f(\\frac{1}{4}(x-1))-8?$",
      "worked_solution": "To perform transformations of functions with multiple operations, we must remember the following rule:\n\n1\\. First, we perform the transformations *inside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out horizontal stretches, followed by horizontal translations.\n\n2\\. Then, we perform the transformations *outside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out vertical stretches, followed by vertical translations.\n\nTo plot $y=\\frac{1}{2}f(\\frac{1}{4}(x-1))-8,$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=f(x).$\n\n- Stretch it by a scale factor of $\\frac{1}{(\\frac{1}{4})}=4$ parallel to the $x$-axis to get the graph of $y=f(\\frac{1}{4}x).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14215685/assets/b6b847be6f77123d3baec5f3541caf2a151039e35a5aad68b0228508d84dbc88.png)\n\n- Then, translate it right by $1$ unit to get the graph of $y=f(\\frac{1}{4}(x-1)).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14215685/assets/8da2b9a2d31c082c069a066709afd5346c702c75a96b840d1c6ee5d9f940bf8f.png)\n\n- Then, stretch it by a scale factor of $\\frac{1}{2}$ parallel to the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=\\frac{1}{2}f(\\frac{1}{4}(x-1)).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14215685/assets/fd1ee07f396bf7561dc93cf4eb5f4098bb0c465c6f4b4a83328751d7e9a65dfa.png)\n\n- Finally, translate it down by $8$ units to get the graph of $y=\\frac{1}{2}f(\\frac{1}{4}(x-1))-8.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14215685/assets/b9f282fc14207257835dbf9ce368d07e68cb207a04875a64cccfe07f31ef5d32.png)",
